BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Girona//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Girona — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Xuixo — Fried laminated dough piped with crema catalana and rolled in sugar\, eaten warm.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SHOO-shoo. Girona's own pastry\, born on Carrer de la Cort Reial\; the sugar must crackle. Best: Can Castelló\, Carrer de l'Argenteria 7 — the shop that fries nothing else
LOCATION:Can Castelló\, Carrer de l'Argenteria 7 — the shop that fries nothing else
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Castello+Carrer+de+l%27Argenteria+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Xocolata desfeta amb melindros — Hot chocolate thick enough to coat the spoon\, with sponge fingers to dip.
DESCRIPTION:Say: shoo-koo-LAH-ta dess-FEH-ta. The granja habit: chocolate as a meal at five in the afternoon. Best: Xocolateria l'Antiga\, under the arcades of Plaça del Vi\, since 1916
LOCATION:Xocolateria l'Antiga\, under the arcades of Plaça del Vi\, since 1916
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Xocolateria+l%27Antiga+Placa+del+Vi+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Botifarra dolça — A pork sausage cured with sugar and lemon peel\, eaten as a sweet.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-tee-FAH-ra DOL-sa. Made only round Girona\; caramelised with apple\, it ends the meal. Best: Mercat del Lleó — the charcuterie stalls\, mornings
LOCATION:Mercat del Lleó — the charcuterie stalls\, mornings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mercat+del+Lleo+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Formatge Garrotxa — Goat's cheese with a grey bloomy rind and a hazelnut finish.
DESCRIPTION:Say: for-MAD-juh ga-RROT-sha. A farmhouse cheese revived in 1981 in the hills north-west of the city. Best: Cal Formatger\, Carrer de la Cort Reial 12 — ask what came in this week
LOCATION:Cal Formatger\, Carrer de la Cort Reial 12 — ask what came in this week
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cal+Formatger+Cort+Reial+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Esmorzar de forquilla — The fork breakfast: cap i pota\, tripe or stewed botifarra\, and a glass of red\, mid-morning.
DESCRIPTION:Say: uz-mor-ZAR de for-KEE-lya. Working Catalonia's second breakfast\, kept alive by the markets. Best: Ca l'Àngel on the Banyoles road\, from six\; or Can Roca in Taialà\, weekday mornings
LOCATION:Ca l'Àngel on the Banyoles road\, from six\; or Can Roca in Taialà\, weekday mornings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ca+l%27Angel+Fontcoberta+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Botifarra amb mongetes — Grilled pork sausage on creamy white beans.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-tee-FAH-ra am moon-JEH-tess. In print by 1830\; round Girona the bean of choice is the small fesol of Santa Pau. Best: Ca l'Àngel\, Fontcoberta — off the grill at breakfast
LOCATION:Ca l'Àngel\, Fontcoberta — off the grill at breakfast
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ca+l%27Angel+Fontcoberta+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Canelons — Pasta rolled round roast meats\, under béchamel\, gratinéed.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ka-nuh-LONS. The 26 December dish\, made all year in the old houses. Best: Casa Marieta\, Plaça de la Independència — the grandmother's recipe\, sold to take away too
LOCATION:Casa Marieta\, Plaça de la Independència — the grandmother's recipe\, sold to take away too
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Casa+Marieta+Placa+de+la+Independencia+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ànec amb peres — Duck braised with pears until both turn amber.
DESCRIPTION:Say: AH-nek am PEH-ress. The old Catalan feast dish of meat with fruit. Best: Casa Marieta — on the card since the old days of the square
LOCATION:Casa Marieta — on the card since the old days of the square
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Casa+Marieta+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arròs a la llauna — Rice baked flat in its tin with rock fish\, small prawns and langoustines.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-ROSS a la LYOW-na. Girona eats its rice dry and from the oven. Best: Fonda Cal Ros\, under the stone vaults of Carrer de la Cort Reial
LOCATION:Fonda Cal Ros\, under the stone vaults of Carrer de la Cort Reial
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fonda+Cal+Ros+Cort+Reial+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cap i pota — Calf's head and trotter stewed until it sets the sauce.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KAP ee POH-ta. Old Girona's stew\, on the card of a bistro run by former Celler cooks. Best: Dit i Fet\, Carrer dels Calderers 10
LOCATION:Dit i Fet\, Carrer dels Calderers 10
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Dit+i+Fet+Calderers+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Gamba de Palamós — The red prawn of the deep canyon\, barely seared or marinated raw.
DESCRIPTION:Say: GAM-ba de pa-la-MOSS. The coast's auction prawn\, an hour away\; Girona's kitchens buy it every day. Best: Esperit Roca — Toda la gamba\, the Celler's 2012 dish\; or Dit i Fet's prawn omelette
LOCATION:Esperit Roca — Toda la gamba\, the Celler's 2012 dish\; or Dit i Fet's prawn omelette
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Esperit+Roca+Sant+Julia+de+Ramis+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Steak tàrtar — Beef tartare carved and dressed in the room.
DESCRIPTION:Say: stek TAR-tar. The dish a sommelier's starred room is known for. Best: Divinum\, Carrer de l'Albareda 7
LOCATION:Divinum\, Carrer de l'Albareda 7
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Divinum+Albareda+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panet — Gelato slid into a warm brioche.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-NET. The way into the Roca universe without a booking. Best: Rocambolesc\, Carrer de Santa Clara
LOCATION:Rocambolesc\, Carrer de Santa Clara
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rocambolesc+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Patates braves — Fried potato cubes under a hot sauce.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-TAH-tess BRAH-vess. A Girona fast-food house of 1973 sells more of them than water. Best: König\, Carrer dels Calderers 16 — until 23:00
LOCATION:König\, Carrer dels Calderers 16 — until 23:00
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Konig+Calderers+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Un negre de l'Empordà — Garnatxa and Carinyena from low\, wind-bent vines.
DESCRIPTION:Say: NEG-ruh de lem-por-DAH. The red of the tramuntana country\, an hour north. Best: Espelt\, Vilajuïga — the estate's own reds\; or any table in this guide
LOCATION:Espelt\, Vilajuïga — the estate's own reds\; or any table in this guide
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Espelt+Viticultors+Vilajuiga+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Garnatxa de l'Empordà — The sweet amber Garnatxa\, the Empordà's dessert wine.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gar-NAT-sha. A protected style\, concentrated on the vine before the ferment is stopped. Best: Espelt\, Vilajuïga — by the half-bottle at the estate
LOCATION:Espelt\, Vilajuïga — by the half-bottle at the estate
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Espelt+Viticultors+Vilajuiga+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vi de porró — Country wine drunk from the long-spouted glass porró.
DESCRIPTION:Say: VEE de pu-RRO. Raise it high and pour without touching the spout. Best: Fonda Cal Ros — the porró of Empordà vi de pagès
LOCATION:Fonda Cal Ros — the porró of Empordà vi de pagès
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Fonda+Cal+Ros+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:girona-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Ratafia — Green-walnut and herb liqueur\, sweet and bitter\, after lunch.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ra-ta-FEE-a. No two family bottles taste alike\; the IGP seal marks the real thing. Best: Can Castelló's ratafia-cream xuixo\, or the house bottle at the end of a meal in the tables
LOCATION:Can Castelló's ratafia-cream xuixo\, or the house bottle at the end of a meal in the tables
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Can+Castello+Girona+Spain
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
